    "title": "AI-Run Modern LaTeX Manuscript Workflow and Replication Packet",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21212502",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-06",
    "description": "<p>This record is the current public workflow and replication packet for the Modern LaTeX Manuscripts project. It describes the actual AI-run process now being used: local source intake, scan/OCR/VLM witness generation, TeX reconstruction, mathematical translation, source-image and object-level auditing, web/pro review handoffs, conservative status labelling, GitHub mirroring, and Zenodo publication.</p>\n<p><strong>Read first:</strong> <code>00_AI_Run_Modern_LaTeX_Manuscript_Workflow_Current_20260706.pdf</code>. That PDF is the front-facing workflow summary. The Markdown source and the ZIP contain supporting addenda, scripts, logs, and cleanup notes.</p>\n<p><strong>Important status rule.</strong> This workflow record is not a critical edition, not proof that any author corpus is complete, and not a certification layer. OCR output, VLM readings, formula crops, first-pass TeX, object detectors, and web-run transcripts are witness and locator layers unless a source-specific audit promotes them. Public author records should distinguish OCR-derived TeX, working drafts, source-witnessed tranches, and critically checked editions.</p>\n<p><strong>Current lesson.</strong> The most reliable pattern is source-first and reader-first: front the PDF or reader a human wants to inspect, put TeX/source/audit/provenance in coherent ZIPs, keep file counts low, use high-resolution scans/crops for hard mathematics and diagrams, use OCR as a prose-completeness witness rather than authority, compile/render-check everything, and publish conservative caveats rather than completion claims.</p>\n<p><strong>Corrections and contributions.</strong> Workflow corrections and reproducibility improvements can be suggested through the GitHub mirror via issues or pull requests: <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
